    "field": "Paleoclimatology",
    "problem": "Existing short observational records of the jet stream hamper the ability to determine if recent increases in weather extremes are unprecedented and to robustly analyze long-term, non-linear climate trends.",
    "method": "The authors combine two temperature-sensitive tree-ring records from the British Isles and the northeastern Mediterranean to reconstruct variability in the latitudinal position of the high-summer North Atlantic Jet (NAJ) back to 1725 CE, placing recent trends in a multi-century context.",
    "task": "The task is to reconstruct the latitudinal variability of the high-summer North Atlantic Jet back to 1725 CE using tree-ring records from Europe to place recent changes in a long-term historical context.",
